(function(){var d={"book": {"chapters": [{"file": "vtm5e-0.5-sortilege-sunburners.lore", "kind": "lore", "name": "# Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition - Path of the Sun (Sortilege Sunburners)", "page": null, "text": "# Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition - Path of the Sun (Sortilege Sunburners)\n# Narrative companion to the Calcinators' Path\n# Version 0.5.3\n#\n# Homebrew (Sortilege), not published material. The rules are in\n# vtm5e-0.5-sortilege-sunburners.ttrpg, which depends on\n# vtm5e-black-hand-walking-the-path; this file carries only what the rules do\n# not need — a Dawn Rite as it happens, how the rest of the Sword sees the Pack,\n# chronicle hooks and sayings. Rewritten 2026-09-22 from the owner's blend\n# decision (vtm5e-conversion/books/sortilege-sunburners/source-blend.md).\n\n## The Furnace\n\nThere is a page in every Calcinator florilegium that is not a formula. It is the\nfirst page, and it says the same thing in every Pack's hand, because the Master\nwho taught the Master who taught this one wrote it out and made them copy it:\n\n*The base matter goes into the fire. What cannot survive the fire leaves as ash.\nWhat can is freed. This is the first operation. It is not the last.*\n\nThe Kindling read it as scripture and as a lab note, and they do not think there\nis a difference. The sun is the furnace. The Embrace put them in it. The Sword of\nCaine has spent seven hundred years pulling the curtains, and the Calcinators\npull them open, because you cannot finish a Work you will not look at. The light\ndevours and the light sustains and it is the same light; the ones it takes were\nnever true, and the ones it leaves are the next thing. They are not proud of\nsurviving. They are proud of being proved.\n\nAsk a Master why the Pack's Advantages name the yellowing and the reddening\nbut not the whitening, and they will tell you that the blackening is the Dawn\nRite itself, and that there is no albedo yet because the Work is not finished.\nThe Sabbat says the Path is unfinished. The Calcinators agree, and think it is\nthe only honest thing the Sword has ever said about them.\n\n## A Dawn Rite\n\nThe roof of a parking structure on the east side of the city, the top deck, no\ncars. Nine Kindling and a fledgling who was a bartender until four hours ago and\nis now sitting on the concrete with her back to a Master called Tallow and her\nhands in his. The Pack is in a ring around them, sitting, all touching, hoodies\noff. Someone has drawn the sun on the deck in sunash and they are inside it.\n\nThe sky goes grey. The fledgling asks what happens now and Tallow tells her the\ntruth, which is that they don't know yet, that's what the morning is for, and\nthat whatever happens nobody is letting go. Somebody starts the litany (*nothing\nis wasted, no one burns alone*) and the rest take it up, not loud yet.\n\nThe rim of the sun comes over the freeway and the first thing that happens is\nthe smell. Nine people begin, quietly, to cook. The fledgling doesn't, not\nstraight away, and Tallow feels her hands go slack with relief and closes his\nown on them harder, because it is the ones who feel nothing at first who are\nlead. Thirty seconds later she screams. She tries to stand and the ring leans in\nand holds her down, and she is thrashing and Tallow is talking into her ear the\nwhole time, the same words, *stay, stay, you're doing it, stay*, and she is\nsmoking now and so is he, so is everyone, and the litany is loud enough to hear\nfrom the street.\n\nShe goes to ash in his arms with the sun a hand's width above the road. The ring\ndoes not let go until the last of her is in his lap. Then they scrape her up\nwith the edges of their hands into a coffee tin, and the youngest of them cries,\nand Tallow says: *she is in the Work now,* and they go downstairs into the dark\nand rub her into their gums.\n\nThe next one lives. That is the other way it goes. Nobody knows which until the\nsun is up, which is the point.\n\n## The Host\n\nThey do not call it Ashe, though they know the word and know the Ashfinders'\nlabs and think them a little soft. Ashe is cooked. The Host is not cooked by\nanyone; it is what the furnace itself left, and the Calcinators hold that this\nis the difference between a drug and a sacrament. It goes into the crucible at\nthe Vaulderie and the whole Pack drinks it, and it goes into the brow before\nRitae, and a Master will keep a pinch of every Packmate the sun has taken in a\nseparate jar with the name on it and will not use those for anything but the\nVaulderie.\n\nAsk a Calcinator whether it bothers them, taking in the ash of someone they held\nan hour ago, and they will look at you as though you have asked whether it\nbothers them to breathe. Nothing is wasted. She is in the Work. Where else\nshould she be?\n\n## How the Sword Sees Them\n\n**Noddists** call them Kindling and mean it as a slur, then sit through one Dawn\nRite and stop. The Devourers' hunt for elder blood and the Calcinators' refusal\nto drink any Cainite at all should make them enemies; in practice the Noddists\nhave decided the Path of the Sun is a heresy they can live beside, because\nnobody who runs Dawn Rites is ever going to compete with them for a Methuselah.\n\n**Cathari** find them tedious and a little frightening. A Devil wants to enjoy\nthe flesh; a Calcinator wants to test it. They share a Resonance, though, and\nmore than one Cathari Pack has bought sun-balm from a Calcinator Pack and paid\nfor it with something the Calcinators wanted more than money.\n\n**Reapers** are the only Sabbat who ask what happens to the Beast when the sun\ntakes a vampire, and they are the only ones the Calcinators will not answer.\n\n**Unifiers** respect the Master's authority and despise the guild's lack of\nhierarchy above it. A Calcinator Pack will not swear to a Bishop. It will trade\nwith one.\n\n**Bahari** understand them better than anyone and are the most careful around\nthem, because the Dark Mother's lesson is that pain teaches and the furnace's\nlesson is that pain selects, and the Lilins can see where that road goes.\n\n**The Camarilla** calls them Sunburners, and a Prince who learns that a\nCalcinator Pack has settled in the domain learns at the same time that every\nthin-blood in it is about to hear a very persuasive offer. Not to join. To be\ntested.\n\n## In Chronicles\n\n- **The coterie's thin-blood is invited to a Dawn Rite.** Not as a fledgling; as\n  a witness. The Pack wants the domain's Duskborn to see what is on offer, and\n  what it costs. Whoever goes comes back changed, or does not come back.\n- **A Calcinator Pack has settled above the redworking scene** and is trading\n  sun-balm for formulae. The local alchemists think they are getting the better\n  of the deal. They are, until the Master asks one of them to come and see the\n  sunrise.\n- **A fledgling survived the Rites who should not have.** Thick blood, an old\n  clan, and she walked out of the light with nothing worse than blisters. The\n  Pack thinks she is the next operation. Her sire thinks she was stolen. The\n  Reapers think she is not what she was.\n- **The Host is running out.** A Pack that has not lost anyone in a season has\n  no sacrament for the Vaulderie, and a Master who lets the crucible go dry is\n  replaced. Somebody is going to be sat facing east, and the Pack is arguing\n  about who.\n- **A jar with a name on it has gone missing** from the Master's shelf, and the\n  Pack will burn the city down to get her back.\n\n## Sayings of the Kindling\n\n- *Nothing is wasted.*\n- *No one burns alone.*\n- *The light devours and the light sustains, and it is the same light.*\n- *What the fire does not take was true.*\n- *Lead does not survive the furnace. Quicksilver does not boil.*\n- *She is in the Work now.*\n- *Pull the curtains. You cannot finish what you will not look at.*\n- *Tried and true.* (said of a Packmate who has stood a Dawn Rite; the highest\n  thing one Calcinator says of another)\n"}, {"container": "EXTENSION", "file": "vtm5e-0.5-sortilege-sunburners.ttrpg", "kind": "ttrpg", "name": "Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition - Path of the Sun (Sortilege Sunburners)", "page": null, "roots": ["#vfbOumVuVYyTGZWpjO8uPpK", "#volV3bUBrhVC5eOlVuXb1QB", "#vmZN2BFOtCXjsJIBVhvuI0g", "#vq7W4gUYtBNTf6eXCS4MPOO"]}], "entities": ["#vfbOumVuVYyTGZWpjO8uPpK", "#volV3bUBrhVC5eOlVuXb1QB", "#vmZN2BFOtCXjsJIBVhvuI0g", "#vq7W4gUYtBNTf6eXCS4MPOO"], "id": "sunburners", "kind": "homebrew", "label": "Path of the Sun: the Sunburners"}, "entities": {"#vK4HjzvFgJqJmj8ozEnxeks": {"aliases": null, "book": "sunburners", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Formulae are the Pack's, not the alchemist's. Any formula known by one Packmate can be distilled by any other Packmate with Thin-Blood Alchemy, using their own method, and the Pack always has Portable Shade and On-Demand Sunburn (see V5 Sabbat pg. 53). Fixatio formulae left in direct sunlight for a full day are distilled at +1 die. Once per Session a thin-blood Packmate may counterfeit any one Level 1 or 2 Discipline power written on a page of the Pack's florilegium without having learned the formula themselves.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-sortilege-sunburners.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vK4HjzvFgJqJmj8ozEnxeks", "key": "The Florilegium", "name": "The Florilegium", "parent": "#vRzjxB25LVPKEpJzzvqJWoP", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vRzjxB25LVPKEpJzzvqJWoP": {"aliases": null, "book": "sunburners", "children": ["#vf9HI0VzQSQxYhjQKtNawsF", "#vsUysqmrzB1zwtfiZCYan3O", "#vf7R3Y1xPpBRQWHnAJc2ozr", "#vK4HjzvFgJqJmj8ozEnxeks", "#vmrIhaoaxJbKDPBvzRJKTVz"], "choices": [], "desc": "The Calcinators are the Sword's cooks and its furnace-tenders. Their formulae are the Pack's property, their crucible is stocked from the dawn, and they have learned to use the sun as equipment rather than survive it as weather. Every Advantage below is the Pack's, as the Black Hand's Paths are (see The Black Hand pg. 15): a character buys one with a number of Path Convictions equal to its cost, and all Packmates get the benefit.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-sortilege-sunburners.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vRzjxB25LVPKEpJzzvqJWoP", "key": "Path of the Sun Advantages", "name": "Path of the Sun Advantages", "parent": "#vfbOumVuVYyTGZWpjO8uPpK", "props": [{"name": "Path Resonance", "type": "STRING", "value": "Choleric. Yellow bile, the humour of fire. Boxers at dawn, the man who set the fire, the woman who will not leave the argument. Heat is an ingredient.", "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vf7R3Y1xPpBRQWHnAJc2ozr": {"aliases": null, "book": "sunburners", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "The yellowing. Packmates with the proper Path Resonance treat direct sunlight as obscured and obscured sunlight as no sunlight at all for the purpose of how often it damages them (see V5 Corebook pg. 221): a thin-blood under a hoodie and sunscreen takes nothing, and a full-blood in the open takes their Bane Severity every other turn. This changes how often sunlight damages them, not whether it provokes Terror Frenzy, and it does not apply during a Ritae: to be tested, you face the furnace.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-sortilege-sunburners.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vf7R3Y1xPpBRQWHnAJc2ozr", "key": "Citrinitas", "name": "Citrinitas", "parent": "#vRzjxB25LVPKEpJzzvqJWoP", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vf9HI0VzQSQxYhjQKtNawsF": {"aliases": null, "book": "sunburners", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "The residue is the Pack's. Packmates with the proper Path Resonance may substitute sunash (see below) for the resonant human blood in any Thin-Blood Alchemy formula. When a Packmate, or a fledgling at the Pack's own Dawn Rites, is destroyed by the sun, every Packmate present takes no Stains for what they did to bring it about, and once per Story heals all Willpower damage.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-sortilege-sunburners.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vf9HI0VzQSQxYhjQKtNawsF", "key": "Caput Mortuum", "name": "Caput Mortuum", "parent": "#vRzjxB25LVPKEpJzzvqJWoP", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vfbOumVuVYyTGZWpjO8uPpK": {"aliases": null, "book": "sunburners", "children": ["#vknFCW7xsnNPk3JerJ2j9ej", "#vRzjxB25LVPKEpJzzvqJWoP"], "choices": [], "desc": "Every alchemist knows the first operation. Calcination: the base matter goes into the furnace, what cannot survive the fire leaves as ash, and what can is freed to be worked. The Calcinators say that Caine's curse is the Great Work performed on a species, that the sun is its furnace, and that the Sword of Caine has spent seven centuries hiding from the one instrument that could finish it. The blood of the Antediluvians is lead: heavy, fixed, and it does not survive the fire. Thin blood is quicksilver: weak, fast, unfixed, and the only vitae in the world that passes through the furnace and comes out proved rather than destroyed. That is the whole of the Path. The light devours and the light sustains, and it is the same light. What it takes, it takes because it was never true, and what it leaves standing is the next thing, tried by the only test that cannot be bribed.\n\nSo the Calcinators do not calcine alone. The Work belongs to a Pack, not to an alchemist: a crucible holds many, and the Pack goes into the furnace together at dawn, holding on to each other and to whoever they Embraced the night before. Those who come out of the light are Kindling. Those who do not are not lost, because nothing is wasted in the Work. The ash of the ones the sun took is the caput mortuum, the dead head, and the Pack takes it back into the vessel as the Host, so that the proved and the consumed are in the same blood. They will destroy any Cainite the Work requires and never drink one, since that is drinking lead, but they will take the residue of anyone the furnace has finished with. Other Sabbat call them a death cult that has stopped pretending. The Calcinators call it the Time of Thin Blood, and mean to be the ones holding the crucible when the Work is done.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-sortilege-sunburners.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vfbOumVuVYyTGZWpjO8uPpK", "key": "Path of the Sun", "name": "Path of the Sun", "parent": null, "props": [{"name": "Roleplay", "type": "STRING", "value": "Alchemical sigils scorched into the skin by the sun through stencils and kept: the sun for gold over the sternum, the operation currently under way on the back of the hand. Mending a mark the furnace gave you is apostasy, so their faces are more keloid than skin. The Host is rubbed into the brow before Ritae. Sunglasses by day and by night, for the eyes rather than the vanity, because they have looked into the furnace on purpose, and beneath them the bloodshot, pitted eyes of the sleepless. Jars of sunash labelled by name, date and horizon. They speak in operations (\"he needs calcining\", \"we'll sublimate that\"), sleep too little, hold a stranger's hand while they explain what is about to happen to them, and their Ritae are loud.", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Nicknames", "type": "STRING", "value": "Calcinators, Kindling, Heliophiles. Outsiders say Sunburners.", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Takbir", "type": "STRING", "value": "*Solve et coagula!, Nothing is wasted!, No one burns alone!, Tried and true!, The sun is the furnace!*", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "The Priesthood", "type": "STRING", "value": "A Calcinator Pack is a guild and its Priest is its Master, and a Master is made in the furnace. The Master sits nearest the east at the Dawn Rites, holds the fledgling's hands, and stands last. Masters keep the Pack's florilegium, the shared book of formulae, and adding a page to it is the highest honour the Path has; a Master who cannot produce what the Pack needs, or who mends a burn the sun gave them, is replaced. Monomacy among Calcinators is an assay: the challengers distil at sunrise, and the one who stays in the light and delivers the formula wins, judged by the Pack on their own bodies. Calcinator Packs are large and slow to move, because a furnace is heavy and a florilegium is precious, and they trade formulae with the redworking scene of any city they settle in until that scene works out what the Pack does at dawn. Jack Dolores ran Dawn Rites before anyone called them that.", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Touchstones", "type": "STRING", "value": "Calcinators connect their Convictions to the Creation Rites (the Dawn Rites, which they call the Calcination), the Fire Dance, or the Vaulderie, whose chalice is the Pack's crucible.", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Frenzy", "type": "STRING", "value": "Calcinators never resist Terror Frenzy from sunlight or fire. The Beast is base matter, and the Pack has taught it where to run: a Packmate with a Beast who frenzies from sunlight or fire Rides the Wave (see V5 Corebook pg. 219), and the frenzy carries them toward the source and into their Packmates' arms rather than away from it. They Ride the Wave of Hunger Frenzy and seek mortal prey. Thin-bloods who cannot frenzy are the Path's proof that quicksilver does not boil.", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Path Compulsion", "type": "STRING", "value": "*Calcination.* The Calcinator must put something into the furnace before the Scene ends: a formula, a vessel, an enemy, themselves, a Packmate's burning taken as their own, or a cherished possession utterly destroyed. They suffer a -3 die penalty to any action for the rest of the Scene that does not involve burning, testing, or transforming something.", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Convictions", "type": "STRING", "value": "Calcinators choose Convictions that put the Work and the Pack before the self, refuse the vitae of Cainites as poison, and treat fire and sun as the only honest tests.", "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vknFCW7xsnNPk3JerJ2j9ej": {"aliases": null, "book": "sunburners", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": null, "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-sortilege-sunburners.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vknFCW7xsnNPk3JerJ2j9ej", "key": "Example Path Convictions", "name": "Example Path Convictions", "parent": "#vfbOumVuVYyTGZWpjO8uPpK", "props": [{"items": [{"value": "Nothing is wasted", "vk": "scalar"}, {"value": "No one burns alone", "vk": "scalar"}, {"value": "Never drink lead", "vk": "scalar"}, {"value": "Test everything by fire", "vk": "scalar"}, {"value": "Share the formula", "vk": "scalar"}, {"value": "Stay until the end", "vk": "scalar"}], "name": "Items", "of": "STRING", "vk": "list"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vmZN2BFOtCXjsJIBVhvuI0g": {"aliases": null, "book": "sunburners", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "The ash of a vampire destroyed by sunlight. The Ashfinders need a laboratory, a flame at 1,500°C and aluminium filings to make Ashe from a vampire's remains. The Calcinators say the sun has already done that work, and done it cleaner: what the dawn leaves behind is calcined, purified, and free of the taint the Path refuses to drink. Sunash from a Pack's own Dawn Rites, or from a Packmate the sun took, is the Host, and it goes into the crucible at the Vaulderie so that the proved and the consumed are in the same blood.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-sortilege-sunburners.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [{"concerns": [{"hash": "#vmZN2BFOtCXjsJIBVhvuI0g", "name": "Sunash"}], "id": "#vNMjcW1dx8JTNnTxnHuj5s7", "name": "The Residue and the Reapers", "text": "The Calcinators say the sun burned the Beast out of the ash, which is why no Shard rises from it. Necronomists who have looked say it went somewhere else, and that the desert festivals where the Heliophiles gather are not as empty as they look. A Storyteller who wants the Path to carry a cost the Pack cannot see coming has one here: what the Reapers find when they go looking is theirs to decide.", "topics": []}], "id": "#vmZN2BFOtCXjsJIBVhvuI0g", "key": "Sunash", "name": "Sunash", "parent": null, "props": [{"name": "System", "type": "STRING", "value": "Sunash is Ashe (see Cults of the Blood Gods pg. 45) that needs no Concoct Ashe and no Fixatio. A destroyed vampire yields one dose per point of Health they had. Any thin-blood can take it as Ashe, snorted, eaten, injected or rubbed into the gums with a Rouse Check's worth of Duskborn vitae. It grants the Ashe effect (Blood Potency counts as 1 for Blood Surges and Discipline Rouse Check re-rolls until the end of the chapter) and carries Ashe Addiction as printed (see Cults of the Blood Gods pg. 46). Sunash can be laced into any Thin-Blood Alchemy formula as an ingredient worth +1 die under the very potent or magical rule (see V5 Corebook pg. 283). Chemically-Induced Flashback and Discipline Channeling (see Cults of the Blood Gods pg. 45-46) work on sunash exactly as on Ashe. No Beast Shard rises from sunash. Taking sunash is not diablerie and incurs no Stains; drinking a Cainite's blood is, and does.", "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vmrIhaoaxJbKDPBvzRJKTVz": {"aliases": null, "book": "sunburners", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "All Packmates can buy Fortitude as if it was a Clan Discipline, including thin-blood Packmates, who may learn and retain Fortitude as if they had the Discipline Affinity Merit for it (see V5 Corebook pg. 183). Once per Story when the Pack Priest performs the Vaulderie at sunrise with the Host in the crucible, every Packmate with the proper Path Resonance mends one Aggravated Health per Rouse Check as though it were Superficial for the rest of the Session and takes no Ashe Addiction from the Host. Bane Severity and the sunlight rules are unchanged. The Calcinators call it the reddening and say it is what the Work looks like finished.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-sortilege-sunburners.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vmrIhaoaxJbKDPBvzRJKTVz", "key": "Rubedo", "name": "Rubedo", "parent": "#vRzjxB25LVPKEpJzzvqJWoP", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#volV3bUBrhVC5eOlVuXb1QB": {"aliases": null, "book": "sunburners", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "The Sabbat buries its fledglings. The Calcinators sit theirs up. The newly Embraced are taken somewhere with a clear eastern horizon, a rooftop, a beach, a salt flat, the top deck of a parking structure, and set facing east with the whole Pack around them, holding on. Nobody leaves until the sun is fully up, and nobody burns alone: the Pack sits in the light with the fledgling and takes what the light gives. Thin-bloods and most Caitiff live, blistered, screaming, half-blind, but standing, and are Kindling from that morning. A fledgling of thicker blood usually does not. They frenzy, they are held, and they burn, and when it is over the Pack gathers what is left of them into the vessel. The Calcinators call it the Calcination, and hold that it is the first operation of the Work performed on a Pack rather than a person.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-sortilege-sunburners.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#volV3bUBrhVC5eOlVuXb1QB", "key": "The Dawn Rites", "name": "The Dawn Rites", "parent": null, "props": [{"name": "System", "type": "STRING", "value": "The Dawn Rites are the Creation Rites (see The Black Hand pg. 62) and count as that Ritae for every purpose, including Touchstone Ritae (see The Black Hand pg. 13). A fledgling who survives them may take a Path Conviction immediately rather than within a month, and attach it to the Creation Rites as its Touchstone Ritae. A fledgling destroyed by the Rites yields sunash. The Pack's Priest needs one dot in the Ritae Advantage as for any Auctoritas Ritae. A Pack that has held its own Dawn Rites at least once may attach its Path Convictions to Ritae Touchstones; until then, its Path of the Sun followers keep mortal Touchstones, as the Black Hand's Lost Paths note describes (see The Black Hand pg. 23).", "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vq7W4gUYtBNTf6eXCS4MPOO": {"aliases": null, "book": "sunburners", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "The Calcinators' Ignoblis Ritae. Each Packmate shows a burn and names the formula or the trial that made it, and the Master reads aloud the page it added to the florilegium while the Pack witnesses. A Packmate with no new mark since the last Assay is expected to earn one before the next. It is often held straight after a Dawn Rite, with the Host still warm.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-sortilege-sunburners.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vq7W4gUYtBNTf6eXCS4MPOO", "key": "The Assay", "name": "The Assay", "parent": null, "props": [{"name": "System", "type": "STRING", "value": "As any Ignoblis Ritae (see The Black Hand pg. 66), the Assay heals each Packmate of one Superficial Willpower damage or changes the Pack's Resonance to Choleric. A formula added to the florilegium at the Assay is an implement of the Vaulderie Touchstone Ritae for any Packmate whose Conviction is attached to it, and its loss is treated as the loss of a Touchstone Ritae implement (see The Black Hand pg. 13).", "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vsUysqmrzB1zwtfiZCYan3O": {"aliases": null, "book": "sunburners", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "When a Packmate takes Aggravated Health damage from fire or sunlight, any other Packmate within reach may take any number of those points in their place, before Fortitude or any other reduction is applied. A Packmate who has taken another's burning this Scene cannot be Impaired by Health damage from fire or sunlight until the Scene ends.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-sortilege-sunburners.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vsUysqmrzB1zwtfiZCYan3O", "key": "No One Burns Alone", "name": "No One Burns Alone", "parent": "#vRzjxB25LVPKEpJzzvqJWoP", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}}, "src": "data/sunburners.js"};var T=window.VTM5E=window.VTM5E||{books:{},entities:{},loaded:{}};
T.loaded[d.src]=true;T.books[d.book.id]=d.book;
for(var h in d.entities){T.entities[h]=d.entities[h];}})();
